    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῡχᾰγωγ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leading departed souls to
				the nether world,</i> epith. of Hermes, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>conjuring up the dead</i> to question them, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. γόοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					687
				</span></i>
			:—Subst., <i>necromancer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.560f
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ψ.,</span></b> 
			οἱ, name of a play by Aeschylus.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>kidnapper,</i> Alexandrian word acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.127
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i></div>
